===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A heavy or helpless collapse; a slouching or drooping [[posture]]; a period of poor activity or performance, especially an [[extended]] period.
## {{lb|en|slang|by|_|extension}} A period when a person goes without the expected amount of [[sex]] or [[date|dating]].
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Jonathan Tolins|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=G6MGnDzibpwC&pg=PA60&dq=slump+sex&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CBsQ6AEwADhkahUKEwjJz5e0t9fIAhVJ5GMKHQxaC4s#v=onepage&q=slump%20sex&f=false|title=The Last Sunday in June
|passage=TOM. We haven't had sex with each other in five months.<br>MICHAEL. We're in a '''slump''', I know that."}}
# A measure of the fluidity of freshly mixed concrete, based on how much the concrete formed in a standard slump cone sags when the cone is removed.
# {{lb|en|geology}} A form of [[mass wasting]] in which a [[coherent]] mass of loosely consolidated materials or a rock layer moves a short distance down a slope.
# {{lb|en|geology|loosely}} A crater or depression (an area where the ground [[slump#Verb|slumps]]) which forms as a result of such wasting. {{q|A large crater is colloquially called a {{m|en|megaslump}}.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2022-09-08|author=Mark Brownlow|author2=Elizabeth White|title=Frozen Planet II|publisher=Random House|isbn=9781473532625
|text=The biggest '''slump''' in the world - a mega-slump - is in the Russian taiga. Known as the Batagaika crater, it is a kilometre-long gash in the ground, about 70 metres deep, and growing{{nb...}}}}
# {{lb|en|UK|dialect}} A [[boggy]] place.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1880|author=William Hugh Patterson|title=A Glossary of Words in Use in the Counties of Antrim and Down
|passage=The road was all '''slumps''' of holes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1911|author=Samuel Rutherford Crockett|title=Rose of the Wilderness|page=165
|passage=It was neither seemly nor befitting that so great an occasion should have its solemnity defaced by leaping-poles or four hands crossed cradlewise to convey the bridal finery over “'''slump'''” or “quakkin'-qua[g]”!}}
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} The noise made by anything falling into a hole, or into a soft, [[miry]] place.
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} The [[gross]] [[amount]]; the [[mass]]; the [[lump]].
# A [[cobbler]]-like [[dessert]] cooked on a [[stove]].
#: ''a blackberry '''slump'''''

